From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: elkir0 <elkir0@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 31 Oct 2026 12:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 23/24] ARM: gts28ltexx: GPU devfreq design (not included in
 the board)

An OPP table for the Mali-T760 (160-700 MHz, stock worst-case voltages
plus a cold margin), panfrost as a devfreq cooling device, and passive
trips on the g3d and apollo thermal zones, with a config fragment for
the devfreq governor and devfreq cooling.  docs/GPU.md section 10 has
the derivation.

Not included by exynos5433-gts28ltexx.dts.  First run on the tablet
(docs/GPU.md section 10.10): clock and BUCK6 voltage follow every OPP,
the governor scales up to 600 MHz under load, the cooling device
registers.  Stability per level is still untested: the GL load used for
the test faults on every job already at the boot clock.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 .../exynos5433-gts28ltexx-gpufreq.dtsi        | 273 ++++++++++++++++++
